parts.stem:
Llamas are mammals that are adapted to live at high altitudes.

Fig. 6.1 shows oxygen dissociation curves for haemoglobin of llamas and humans.

{{figure:figure-6-1-source.png}}

parts.text:
The partial pressure of oxygen in the lungs of mammals at 3500 m is 6.4 kPa.

Use Fig. 6.1 to state the percentage saturation of haemoglobin of llamas and humans at an oxygen partial pressure of 6.4 kPa.

{{figure:reviewed_response_3.png}}
